Package: ggplotify
Title: Convert Almost Any Plot to a 'grob' or 'ggplot' Object
Version: 0.1.4
Authors@R: c(person("Guangchuang", "Yu", email = "guangchuangyu@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6485-8781")))
Description: Convert a plot to a 'grob' or a 'ggplot' object so that it joins the
    'grid' and 'ggplot2' ecosystem. The input can be a plot call written as a
    formula or an expression, a function that draws to a graphics device, a
    graphic object produced by another package, or a plot captured by
    'grDevices::recordPlot'. Output of 'base' graphics is redrawn with
    'gridGraphics', so plots from different graphics systems can be arranged,
    aligned, annotated and inset with packages such as 'aplot' and 'patchwork'.
Depends: R (>= 3.4.0)
Imports: ggplot2, graphics, grDevices, grid, gridGraphics, rlang,
        utils, yulab.utils
Suggests: aplot, colorspace, ggimage, knitr, lattice, patchwork,
        quarto, testthat, vcd
